      "findings": [
        {
          "id": "AV1",
          "check": "api",
          "finding": "Figma Background (Neutral, Brand, Success, Warning, Danger) has no attribute. Figma binds Neutral color.neutral.surface with color.neutral.foreground initials; Brand color.action.default with color.text.on-action; Success, Warning, and Danger color.<tone>.surface with color.<tone>.foreground. Every token exists.",
          "proposal": "A colour attribute (decision D1), each value drawing Figma's pair of tokens."
        },
        {
          "id": "AV2",
          "check": "api",
          "finding": "Figma Background=Custom takes any HEX fill on the avatar, with the initials colour overridable on its own. The element offers only ::part(base).",
          "proposal": "CSS custom properties --odd-avatar-background and --odd-avatar-color (per instance through style, for example a colour from user data). The guidance says the author owns the contrast of a custom pair."
        },
        {
          "id": "AV3",
          "check": "api",
          "finding": "Figma Shape (Square radius.none, Small radius radius.sm, Rounded radius.md, Circle radius.full) has no attribute; avatar.structural.styles.ts hard-codes border-radius: 50%.",
          "proposal": "A shape attribute (decision D2), and --odd-avatar-radius for any other radius."
        },
        {
          "id": "AV4",
          "check": "visual",
          "finding": "Two Figma families disagree on the default look. avatar/Appearance draws Neutral as color.neutral.surface with color.neutral.foreground, and 32 px initials in the UI type. The older avatar State=Initials (the one the parity test compares) binds color.surface.sunken with color.text.primary, and the code follows it, with the small type at size sm.",
          "proposal": "Decision D3. Then the default draws the current family and the other is updated in Figma."
        },
        {
          "id": "AV5",
          "check": "visual",
          "finding": "Figma's AvatarItem draws a border.width.strong ring in color.surface.default on every avatar. The code rings avatars only inside .odd-avatar-group, as a box-shadow in color.canvas.",
          "proposal": "Keep the ring for groups only, where it separates overlapping avatars (on the default surface a lone avatar's ring cannot be seen), recorded as a deliberate difference; draw it in Figma's color.surface.default."
        },
        {
          "id": "AV6",
          "check": "visual",
          "finding": "Sizes match: Figma Small 32, Medium 40, Large 48 px are control.height.sm, md, and lg; size is sm, md, or lg.",
          "proposal": "None."
        },
        {
          "id": "AV7",
          "check": "parity",
          "finding": "The parity tests compare only avatar State=Initials (md and sm) and the multiselect avatars view. Not compared: the 24 Appearance variants, the Group variant (.odd-avatar-group and .odd-avatar-group-more), the ring.",
          "proposal": "Compare every Background and Shape variant, and the group, in light and dark, with the fix."
        },
        {
          "id": "AV8",
          "check": "a11y",
          "finding": "Not yet measured: the contrast of each preset's initials on its fill, in light and dark. Forced colours: the element draws a 1px CanvasText border, which must follow every shape.",
          "proposal": "Measure each pair (at least 4.5:1 for the initials) with the fix."
        },
        {
          "id": "AV9",
          "check": "docs",
          "finding": "Examples cover sizes, a picture, an overflow count, an avatar beside a name, and name versus label; none shows a colour, a shape, a custom colour, or a group.",
          "proposal": "An example per new value, one with a custom colour, and a group with its overflow avatar."
        },
        {
          "id": "AV10",
          "check": "figma",
          "finding": "For the owner, in Figma: (a) the review row's \"Large · 12 px\" is an instance of Shape=Rounded with its radius overridden to radius.lg, and there is no Large shape; (b) the Appearance set's default variant is Square, while AvatarItem and the older family are circles; (c) Custom's initials bind repo/ref/neutral/0, a reference colour, not a role token.",
          "proposal": "Decide (a) and (b) with D2; bind (c) to a role, or leave the custom foreground to the author."
        }
      ],
      "decisions": [
        {
          "id": "D1",
          "question": "The colour attribute: name and values.",
          "options": [
            "tone=\"neutral | brand | info | success | warning | danger\": ADR 0045's meaning-colour name, with brand added for the avatar and info kept so it matches odd-badge and odd-alert (Figma has no Info avatar yet).",
            "tone with ADR 0045's values only (no brand), and the brand look stays the .odd-avatar-group-more recipe."
          ],
          "recommendation": "The first: one attribute with the vocabulary's name, every Figma preset reachable, the same tones as odd-badge; ADR 0045 records brand as an avatar tone.",
          "answer": null
        },
        {
          "id": "D2",
          "question": "The shape attribute: name, values, and default.",
          "options": [
            "shape=\"circle | rounded | small-radius | square\", Figma's Shape values, default circle (today's look and AvatarItem's).",
            "radius=\"none | sm | md | full\", the radius token names."
          ],
          "recommendation": "The first: Figma's property name and values, as button's appearance follows Figma; default circle. Any other radius (the review row's 12 px) through --odd-avatar-radius.",
          "answer": null
        },
        {
          "id": "D3",
          "question": "Which Figma avatar is current: avatar/Appearance (the one linked on 2026-11-15) or the older avatar State=Initials?",
          "options": [
            "avatar/Appearance; the older Initials variant is updated or removed in Figma.",
            "The older avatar."
          ],
          "recommendation": "avatar/Appearance: Neutral becomes color.neutral.surface with color.neutral.foreground, and 32 px initials keep the UI type.",
          "answer": null
        }
      ],
      "audited": "2026-11-15",
      "summary": "Figma draws five preset backgrounds, a custom HEX background, and four corner radii (Oddkin/Common/avatar/Appearance, 374:1576; the review row 374:1580). odd-avatar has neither: it always draws a sunken circle with primary-text initials. Sizes match."
